# solar-ctl A/B layout (doc swupdate-ota.md §5, §10 step 4).
#
# This is a wic TEMPLATE (.wks.in): image_types_wic expands the ${VARS}
# below from the IMAGE recipe's datastore at build time. The geometry
# constants live in classes/solar-ablayout.bbclass (inherited by
# solar-ctl-image.bb) and are shared with the U-Boot env kconfig fragment
# and /etc/fw_env.config - the layout moves as one unit or not at all.
# Undefined ${VAR}s would be stripped silently by the expander, so every
# name here must exist in the class.
#
#  p1 vfat    GPU firmware + u-boot.bin (deployed as kernel.img) + boot.scr
#             + uImage (factory fallback only). Per-slot kernels
#             live on ext4 /data/cores/slot-{a,b} since 2026-09-28, NOT on
#             p1. The U-Boot env left p1 on 2026-10-05 (see the hidden part
#             below): slot switches no longer write FAT metadata at all,
#             and Linux never needs to mount p1 rw.
#  hidden     raw redundant U-Boot env pair (uboot-env-redundant.bin from
#             solar-uboot-env, copied by rawcopy out of DEPLOY_DIR_IMAGE),
#             --no-table: written into the image at --offset but absent from
#             the partition table (msdos primary slots are all taken by
#             p1..p4; a table entry for 32 KiB would also tempt resize
#             tools). Consequence: slot-a lands at 108 MiB (p1 = 4..104,
#             env 32 KiB flush at 104, then --align 4096 rounding) -
#             invisible: p2/p3/p4 keep their indexes and every consumer
#             addresses them by index. (NB: pre-fixed-size images from
#             2026-09 actually had p1 at 4..134 MiB and slot-a at 136 MiB -
#             see the --fixed-size gotcha below - also harmless for the
#             same index reason.) Never
#             mounted, never in any fstab; Linux touches it only through
#             fw_setenv/libubootenv. Copy0 @ offset, copy1 @ offset+16 KiB
#             (offsets derived in the class; u-boot's ENV_OFFSET(_REDUND)
#             and fw_env.config read the same two numbers).
#  p2/p3      squashfs-xz root slots, FIXED size: the payload must fit or
#             the wic build fails (there is no resize at flash time).
#  p4 ext4    /data: mounted by the overlayfs-etc preinit, hosts the /etc
#             overlay upper and app state. Deliberately given no mountpoint
#             in the wks -> no fstab line, so systemd never owns the mount.
#             NB: NO --source here - "--source empty" leaves the partition
#             UNFORMATTED (all zeros); no source at all is what makes wic
#             run mkfs.ext4 on it.
#
# --size/--fixed-size are in MiB, --offset/--align are in KiB. Slots:
# ~350 MiB as in the design doc.
# p4 is sized for the 122 GB bench card (any slack stays unpartitioned at
# the end of the card; a smaller card fails the wic build with a clear
# error - adjust --fixed-size if the card changes).
#
# TRAP (hit 2026-10-05, caught by the hidden env part colliding): p1 MUST
# be --fixed-size, never plain --size. wic's default overhead_factor=1.3 is
# applied to every non-fixed part during content sizing: a --size 100 p1
# silently becomes 130 MiB (get_rootfs_size: content padded to the request,
# then x1.3), which walked over the --offset of the hidden env area and
# killed do_image_wic with "Could not place mmcblk02 at offset 109051904".
# --fixed-size bypasses the overhead math entirely (and overflows fail
# loudly), so the p1 geometry the class derives stays what the card gets.
# Boot content is ~20 MiB; 100 fixed has ample headroom.

part /boot --source bootimg-partition --ondisk mmcblk0 --fstype=vfat --label boot --active --align ${SOLAR_BOOT_ALIGN_KB} --fixed-size ${SOLAR_BOOT_SIZE_MB} --fsoptions "defaults,ro"
part --source rawcopy --sourceparams "file=${SOLAR_UBOOT_ENV_BLOB}" --ondisk mmcblk0 --no-table --offset ${SOLAR_UBOOT_ENV_OFFSET_KB}
# (squashfs has no label concept - wic refuses --label here; the slots are
#  addressed as /dev/mmcblk0p{2,3}, per doc §4's device-node root= decision)
part slot-a --source rootfs --ondisk mmcblk0 --fstype=squashfs --align 4096 --fixed-size 350 --mkfs-extraopts "-comp xz"
part slot-b --source rootfs --ondisk mmcblk0 --fstype=squashfs --align 4096 --fixed-size 350 --mkfs-extraopts "-comp xz"
part none --ondisk mmcblk0 --fstype=ext4 --label data --align 4096 --fixed-size 119000
